{! Hat Trick Text Template — grammar sampler.
   Open in the editors/vscode F5 dev host to eyeball how every tag family
   highlights. This is a highlighting fixture, not a rendering test. }

Hello {Name.First} {Name.Last},

{#if Account.IsActive}
Your account has been active since {Account.MemberSince}.

{#each Account.Orders}
  - Order {$.Id}: {$.Total} placed {$.PlacedOn}
{/each}
{/if}

{#with Account.Address}
Ship to: {Line1}, {City} {State} {Zip}   ({..\Account.Region})
{/with}

{! variables: declare, reassign, read }
{?var:greeting = "Thanks"}
{?:greeting = "Thank you"}
{:greeting} for being a member, {$.Name.First}.

{! lambda call and literals }
Total due: {Invoice.Lines.((line, acc) => sumTotals)}
Flags: {true}, {false}, {null}, {42}, {-3.14}

{! trim markers lead/trail a block tag }
{-#each Notices}
{$.Text}
{/each-}

{! partial include, then a debug tag }
{>footer-signature}
{@Account.Address}

{! escaped braces render literally — not tags }
Use {{ and }} for a literal brace, e.g. {{ not a tag }} but {Name} is.
